      "writtenOn": "2023-03-27T15:32:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The read sends back all bytes (port 0 and port 1) by definition.  So all reads to the emulator will give 3 bytes, but the third byte representing port 1 is currently zeroed out.  \n\nAnd for fun, the \"port 1\" on this mux doesn\u0027t at all correspond to our \"port 1\" from the Chromebook perspective.  Our port 0 is on port 0 of one i2c address, and our port 1 is on port 0 of the other i2c address for the mux, so the driver is currently hard coded to only ever interact with port 0",
      "parentUuid": "6560f5c1_7b1634fb",
      "revId": "96b88b421b2fe9a14303ce477032a3640ad6caa0",
